  "how_to_read": {
    "cases": "Each case adds target_json (raw JSON text) to the intent target of the base payloads, or sets an option. Inputs are generated per run with fresh synthetic keys; every producer signs the same input bytes.",
    "modes": "bytes: each piece is given to the producer as its original bytes. value: the producer's own JSON decoder reads the bytes into a host value first.",
    "ring": "R: the base assembled by each producer from the artifacts the next producer signed (ts, py, go, rust, wasm, ts), received as bytes.",
    "negatives": "Byte edits of each producer's fresh output, then verified by every consumer; post-signature mutations reach the candidate verifier and fail.",
    "decoder_calls": "How many times the consumer's historical decoder was called, observed by the adapter: 1 for a unit the scanner cannot walk (BOM, UTF8_INVALID, SYNTAX), 0 for every other rejection and for every candidate."
  },
